Anatomy kit vendored into third_party/anatomy.

Upstream: https://github.com/wheresryan22/anatomy
License: MIT (see LICENSE)
Copyright (c) 2026 Ryan

Vendored files:
- kit/iso-kit.mjs   (isometric SVG geometry + shading)
- kit/lathe.mjs     (profile / curve math used by audit.mjs)
- kit/tube.mjs      (tube path math used by audit.mjs)
- kit/audit.mjs     (geometry audit: no clipping, every endpoint supported, draw order)
- kit/gl.mjs        (optional WebGL shader camera — unused by Hevi render path)
- kit/canvas-painter.mjs (turning 3D painter — unused by Hevi render path)
- scripts/capture.mjs  (headless Chrome screenshot)
- scripts/drive.mjs    (headless Chrome driver: wait, shot, lines, slow-motion)
- scripts/lines.mjs    (floating-line check, wraps drive.mjs)
- scripts/chrome-port.mjs
- scripts/inline-kit.mjs (embeds kit source into a standalone page)
- scripts/line-ends.mjs (floating-line detection used by drive.mjs lines action)

Hevi uses these only to build static isometric SVG figures, run the upstream
geometry audit (audit.mjs) and the floating-line check (lines.mjs), and to
drive headless Chrome (CPU / SwiftShader) for frame-by-frame video rendering.
No changes were made to the vendored logic; only relative imports are kept
intact. The 3D beta mode and WebGL shaders are intentionally out of scope.

This product bundles the Anatomy kit (MIT). The rest of the Hevi worktree is
governed by its own license.
